From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 20:41:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] layer-shell: refresh focus on input-region changes

Layer-shell clients often expand their surface input region while a menu or popover is open, then shrink it again
from the button-press handler that dismisses the menu. If the pointer stays stationary, Clutter's sprite keeps the
old current actor until the next motion event. Wayland pointer focus is then synced from that stale actor, so the
next click can still be delivered to the closed menu surface even though the committed input region no longer
contains that coordinate.

Invalidate the current stage focus whenever a surface actor's input region changes. This forces a pick at the
sprite's current coordinates using the new input shape, so stale focus is cleared without requiring pointer motion.
A cached clear area may belong to an underlying surface while an overlay expands its input region, so refresh
every view on region changes, retaining the immediate focused-surface update for shrinking regions.
---
 clutter/clutter/clutter-stage-private.h |  2 ++
 src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c     | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage-private.h b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage-private.h
index bb9141cc..f2338443 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage-private.h
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage-private.h
@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ void clutter_stage_unlink_grab (ClutterStage *self,
 void clutter_stage_invalidate_focus (ClutterStage *self,
                                      ClutterActor *actor);
 
+CLUTTER_EXPORT
 void clutter_stage_maybe_invalidate_focus (ClutterStage *self,
                                            ClutterActor *actor);
 
@@ -140,6 +141,7 @@ ClutterGrab * clutter_stage_grab_input_only_inactive (ClutterStage        *self,
                                                       gpointer             user_data,
                                                       GDestroyNotify       user_data_destroy);
 
+CLUTTER_EXPORT
 void clutter_stage_invalidate_devices (ClutterStage *stage);
 
 GPtrArray * clutter_stage_get_active_gestures_array (ClutterStage *self);
diff --git a/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c b/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
index 472be859..2fb2d2a3 100644
--- a/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "compositor/meta-surface-actor.h"
 
 #include "clutter/clutter.h"
+#include "clutter/clutter-stage-private.h"
 #include "compositor/clutter-utils.h"
 #include "compositor/meta-background-effect.h"
 #include "compositor/meta-cullable.h"
@@ -738,6 +739,9 @@ meta_surface_actor_set_input_region (MetaSurfaceActor *self,
 {
   MetaSurfaceActorPrivate *priv =
     meta_surface_actor_get_instance_private (self);
+  gboolean changed;
+
+  changed = !mtk_region_equal (priv->input_region, region);
 
   g_clear_pointer (&priv->input_region, mtk_region_unref);
 
@@ -745,6 +749,22 @@ meta_surface_actor_set_input_region (MetaSurfaceActor *self,
     priv->input_region = mtk_region_ref (region);
   else
     priv->input_region = NULL;
+
+  if (changed)
+    {
+      ClutterActor *actor = CLUTTER_ACTOR (self);
+      ClutterActor *stage = clutter_actor_get_stage (actor);
+
+      if (stage)
+        {
+          /* Expanding an input region can cover a sprite focused on another
+           * actor. Its cached clear area must be rebuilt too, not just the
+           * sprites already focused on this surface. */
+          clutter_stage_invalidate_devices (CLUTTER_STAGE (stage));
+          clutter_stage_schedule_update (CLUTTER_STAGE (stage));
+          clutter_stage_maybe_invalidate_focus (CLUTTER_STAGE (stage), actor);
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 void
